From 68622f532e7a3f1c1304bc6e8a2add6629e832d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JavaZeroo <2487163254@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:42:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep torch.distributed.checkpoint/fsdp out of
 torch_npu's import footprint

torch_npu is imported from inside `import torch` (device-backend autoload),
so every module it imports at init time is imported by every `import torch`.
Two init-time imports pulled in torch.distributed.checkpoint and
torch.distributed.fsdp:

1. torch_npu.distributed.tensor imported register_sharding / placement
   types from torch.distributed._tensor, the deprecated alias package whose
   __init__ imports _shards_wrapper -> torch.distributed.checkpoint -> fsdp.
2. the distributed patch group imported torch.distributed.fsdp.sharded_grad_scaler
   eagerly to replace ShardedGradScaler.

On torch >= 2.14 nightly, fsdp's _fsdp_state imports the third-party
spmd_types package at module level. A program whose first torch import
happens *from inside spmd_types* (e.g. `import spmd_types` before
`import torch`, as torchtitan does) then fails with

  RuntimeError: Failed to load the backend extension: torch_npu
  AttributeError: partially initialized module 'spmd_types' has no
  attribute 'register_local_autograd_function' (most likely due to a
  circular import)

Fixes:
- use the public modules (torch.distributed.tensor,
  torch.distributed.tensor.experimental, torch.distributed.tensor._dtensor_spec),
  which do not pull the checkpoint/fsdp chain; the names exist on every
  torch line this tree supports.
- defer the ShardedGradScaler replacement until the user imports
  torch.distributed.fsdp.sharded_grad_scaler (new helper
  torch_npu/utils/_import_hooks.py::run_after_import, a meta-path
  post-import hook; the patch still applies the first time the module is
  imported from anywhere).

Test: test/test_autoload.py::AutoloadImportFootprintTest asserts that
`import torch` (with autoload) does not load torch.distributed.checkpoint
or torch.distributed.fsdp, and that ShardedGradScaler is still replaced
once the module is imported.

Upstream-PR: https://gitcode.com/Ascend/pytorch/merge_requests/45529
Upstream-Issue: https://gitcode.com/Ascend/pytorch/issues/4441
